From cf77e81b97f647c3b72c105a5e7114fb98b601c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 03:16:38 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] Port bun to ppc64le (POWER8+, little-endian, glibc)

`bun --version`, `bun run` of a non-trivial TypeScript script, `bun install`,
`bun build`, `bun test` and `Bun.serve` all run natively on a POWER9 AC922.
No emulation: the binary is `ELF 64-bit LSB executable, PowerPC64, OpenPOWER
ELF V2 ABI`.

JSC comes from a local WebKit checkout (oven-sh/WebKit plus the ppc64le-port
branch's native offlineasm PPC64 LLInt); there is no ppc64le prebuilt tarball,
so `cfg.webkit` defaults to "local" on this arch and $BUN_WEBKIT_PATH points at
the checkout. Verified against the generated LLIntAssembly.h:
OFFLINE_ASM_PPC64 && !OFFLINE_ASM_C_LOOP -- a real PowerPC interpreter, not the
CLoop.

Build system
- config.ts: `Arch` gains "ppc64le"; node spells the host "ppc64", so
  detectHost maps it. `cfg.ppc64le` joins x64/arm64. tinycc off, webkit
  defaults to local, linux sysroot arch string added.
- config.ts: the compiler, not process.arch, decides the arch on Linux too.
  ppc64le has no native bun to bootstrap from, so the build driver is an
  x86_64 bun under an emulator; os.arch() reports the emulated process and the
  build silently targeted linux-x64. Windows already had this workaround for
  the same reason; it now also corrects host.arch, which feeds `isCross` and
  `canRunOnHost`.
- rust.ts: powerpc64le-unknown-linux-gnu triple, and a clang-to-LLVM CPU-name
  map. `clang -mcpu=power9` is accepted by the driver but rustc rejects
  `-Ctarget-cpu=power9` with a *warning*, so without the map the Rust half
  would have quietly built for generic ppc64 while the C++ half built for
  POWER9. LLVM spells it pwr9.
- flags.ts -mcpu/-mtune=power9; codegen.ts TARGET_ARCH=ppc64;
  buildOptionsRs.ts ENABLE_TINYCC=false on target_arch="powerpc64".
- webkit.ts: ENABLE_JIT/FTL/WEBASSEMBLY/SAMPLING_PROFILER off, ENABLE_C_LOOP
  explicitly OFF (the native LLInt is not CLoop), and USE_SYSTEM_MALLOC=OFF --
  WebKitFeatures.cmake puts every non-x86_64/arm64/riscv64 CPU in a fallback
  branch that forces the system allocator on, which collides with bun's
  USE_MIMALLOC ("libpas, mimalloc, and system malloc are exclusive"). libpas is
  the one that genuinely cannot build here; mimalloc is portable, so take the
  route riscv64 takes.
- zlib.ts: portable-C kernels. libjpeg-turbo.ts: upstream's AltiVec SIMD --
  WITH_SIMD is defined unconditionally, so something must supply the jsimd_*
  dispatcher or the final link fails with ~40 undefined symbols.
- New conditional dep patches (identity unchanged for x64/arm64):
  boringssl target.h #errors on unknown CPUs, so crypto_word_t/BN_ULONG were
  never defined (~8000 errors over 176 TUs); mimalloc's mi_atomic_pause()
  #else fallback calls names that only exist in its C++ shim and so does not
  compile from C on any arch lacking its own arm.

Runtime and codegen
- workaround-missing-symbols.cpp: GLIBC_2.17 is the ppc64le symver base
  (verified with objdump -T on libm.so.6), and __wrap_ naming must apply here
  because flags.ts wraps on every linux-gnu arch. _STAT_VER is 3, measured:
  __xstat/__fxstat accept 1 and 3 and return EINVAL for 0 and 2, and both
  accepted values fill an identical struct stat. (An earlier survey claimed 3
  would fail with EINVAL; it does not.)
- CPUFeatures: HWCAP/HWCAP2 feature set (altivec, vsx, POWER8/9/10, crypto),
  matched bit-for-bit across the Rust/C++ FFI boundary.
- platform/linux.rs raw_syscall6 goes through libc::syscall on PowerPC and
  re-encodes to -errno: PowerPC signals syscall failure out-of-band via CR0.SO
  rather than returning a negative errno in-band, and hand-rolling that is easy
  to get subtly wrong.
- Architecture::Ppc64le (npm and node both spell it "ppc64"), crash-handler
  platform tag, ELF interpreter map (ld64.so.2), os.endianness()/os.machine().
- `bun upgrade` names the arch honestly so it 404s instead of installing an
  x86-64 binary over a working ppc64le one.

Features unavailable on ppc64le, each gated rather than left broken
- bun:ffi cc(): oven-sh/tinycc has no PowerPC code generator. dlopen() still
  works; cc() throws "not available in this build".
- WebAssembly: offlineasm has no PPC64 lowering for InPlaceInterpreter.asm, so
  ENABLE_WEBASSEMBLY=OFF. bun forced JSC's useWasm/useBBQJIT on
  unconditionally, which made Options::assertOptionsAreCoherent() abort the
  process at startup; those now follow the ENABLE() macros, whose defaults were
  already right.
- CPU profiler (--cpu-prof, v8::CpuProfiler, bun:jsc sampling): JSC's
  MachineContext has no PPC64 arm.
- Raw-V8-API native addons: PPC64 is the one architecture whose V8 exit frame
  carries a constant-pool slot, so bun's frame indices legitimately disagree
  with real V8's. Node-API (napi) addons are unaffected.
